    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_AS_READ",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 1.19,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.1,
    "rationale": "The undiluted readings plateau at about 1.16 from 8 h onward, which could mean either stationary phase or detector saturation. I checked this by diluting the 18 h aliquot. At 10x the reading was 0.1185, which scales to 1.185. At 3x it was 0.4024, which scales to 1.207. Both are within about 2–4% of the undiluted 1.161. If the reader were saturating, the dilution-corrected values would be clearly higher than the undiluted reading, and they are not. The plateau therefore looks like genuine stationary phase, and the undiluted readings represent the biomass. I used single replicates per dilution, so the small excess over the undiluted reading is within plausible noise."
  },
